---
import TrustPageLayout from '@/layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro'
---

<TrustPageLayout
  title="Privacy | xtarter"
  description="What the xtarter docs site measures: cookieless Umami analytics loaded only when configured, aggregate events, and GitHub avatar fetches for the contributors page. No cookies, no ads."
  eyebrow="xtarter · privacy"
  heading="No cookies. No ads. Just counts."
  lede="This site measures usage in aggregate to decide what to document better, and it is built to touch as little of your data as possible."
>
  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies. There is no login, no comments, and nothing here stores
      identifiers in your browser. The docs are fully static.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">Usage measurement (Umami)</h2>
    <ul class="xt-checklist">
      <li>
        Page views are measured with Umami, a cookieless analytics tool hosted at
        umami.sznm.dev.
      </li>
      <li>
        The analytics script loads only when the site build has UMAMI_SRC and UMAMI_WEBSITE_ID
        configured. Without them it never loads.
      </li>
      <li>
        Aggregate click and change events (hero buttons, theme toggles, search opens) go
        through the same Umami instance.
      </li>
      <li>Measurement is aggregate: no advertising profiles are built from this data.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">GitHub avatars and API</h2>
    <p>
      The contributors page loads contributor avatars from avatars.githubusercontent.com and
      queries api.github.com for metadata. Those requests go from your browser directly to
      GitHub; this site keeps no copy of them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="xt-section">
    <h2 class="xt-section-title">No ads, no data sales</h2>
    <p>
      This site runs no advertising and sells no data. Nothing collected here goes to ad
      networks or data brokers; there is nothing to share beyond anonymous, aggregate
      counters.
    </p>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy? Open an issue at{' '}
      <a
        class="xt-link"
        href="https://github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarter/issues"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >github.com/agustinusnathaniel/xtarter/issues</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</TrustPageLayout>
